% The sources of the library: its one bibliography.
%
% The key of an entry is the key by which everything cites the source: the docstrings and
% comments ([Hir64, Main Theorem I], [Wlo05, §4.6]), among them the paragraphs
% `Source statement: [KEY, locator, page]` of the theorems that formalize an item of a source, the
% blueprint and the Markdown files. Item numbers in citations
% ([Kol07, Theorem 68]) are the source's own. 
%
% What reads this file:
% - scripts/sync_formalization.lean checks that each `Source statement:` paragraph cites a key of
%   this file, and writes the key as the authors' last names and the year ("Hironaka 1964") in the
%   alignment table of formalization.yaml.
% - blueprint/Blueprint/References.lean registers every entry for the blueprint's citations
%   ({cite Hir64}[Main Theorem I] in the chapters, [Hir64, Main Theorem I] in the annotation items
%   taken from docstrings) and its bibliography, which lists the entries the blueprint cites.
% - scripts/check_references.py checks that a source is listed here exactly when some file of the
%   package cites it.
% - scripts/check_formalization_yaml.py compares the sources of formalization.yaml with the
%   entries of the same title (and their authors).
% - scripts/build_docs.py gives this file to doc-gen4 for the bibliography of the API
%   documentation (doc-gen4 reads only ASCII keys, so the script stands in for the others).
%
% To add a source: add its entry here and cite it (the check fails on an entry that nothing
% cites). To drop a source, delete its entry with its last citation.
%
% The file is written in the part of BibTeX that all of these read: an entry is
% `type{key, field = {value}, ...}` after the at sign, a value is in braces or is a bare number,
% accented letters are written as Unicode characters (no TeX macros), and braces protect
% capitals in titles. These comments go between entries, on lines starting with a percent sign,
% and never contain the at sign, which starts an entry.

